      "content": "I like the contrast with the \"day-light reason\" bit. To really lean into that \"untamed\" vibe, I want to push the cultural side more. If they don't have laws or scriptures, what kind of values do they actually hold? Like, do they have certain traits that make them more \"natural\" or \"instinctual\" in a way that might even make them seem less \"human\" or more \"savage\" to the civilized people? I'm trying to figure out if they have certain personality tropes or even certain ethnic-looking characteristics that would make a reader immediately think of them as \"other\" or \"unpredictable.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
